From e86b7b9f92ce881f4bfd740a72fb6de757dfeff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:39:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/32] (b) v2, part b-3: \@kernel@caption@reset ends the
 settings of \caption*

Round-3 finding R3-M1: clsguide told code that keeps its own \caption
and passes only \caption* to the kernel to call two internals,
\@caption@nostep@restore and \@captionstarfalse, in its numbered
\caption. Any setting added to \@caption@nostep@defs later would have
broken such code silently.

\@kernel@caption@reset is now the one command for this: it undoes
everything \@caption@nostep@defs set (\theH<type>, \fnum@<type>,
\ext@<type>; a pending give-back of the unique number is dropped, since
a replaced \@caption may have used it), sets \if@captionstar false and
\if@captionstep and \if@captiontarget true (the state outside a
caption). The kernel \caption starts with it (so \@caption@process no
longer restores and sets the switches itself; same behaviour), the float
first aid uses it, and clsguide shows it in an example. It is defined
together with \@kernel@caption, and undefined by a roll-back.

ltfloat.dtx now says why the settings outlive \caption*: \@caption has
to stay the last token of \caption (float looks for an optional argument
after it), so the kernel gets no control back after it, and a replaced
\@caption may defer its work (threeparttable executes the stored call
at the start of the tabular).

Tests: caption-interface-001 TEST 31 (the reset undoes the settings
and the give-back, resets the switches) and TEST 32 (a package \caption
that routes only the star to \@kernel@caption*: its numbered caption
after \caption* has label, list entry and its own target);
caption-interface-002 shows it undefined after the roll-back. Hook
dumps: the .tlg of 15 lthooks and 2 lthooks2 tests show the new code of
package/float/after (only that line changes).
